  <prompt>
    Author the single Communication ADR — **ADR-045** — that anchors all of R4. It codifies four things as one coherent decision:
    1. **Client canonical send** — one `&lt;EmailComposer /&gt;` engine + three thin wrappers (`SendEmailStep`/`SendEmailDialog`/`SendEmailPage`) + `sendCommunication()` typed wrapper; no ad-hoc/inline send.
    2. **Server Association Engine** — operates over a normalized message envelope (never `Microsoft.Graph.Message`); deterministic-first rung ladder (0–3), then semantic (4) + AI (5); per-attribute confidence + provenance; eight association targets.
    3. **Direction-agnostic enrichment service** — `ICommunicationEnrichmentService` invoked by BOTH inbound and outbound paths (association → categorization → AI → RAG → Responsive Intelligence).
    4. **Channel seams** — `ICommunicationChannelSender` / `ICommunicationArchiver` defined (not implemented beyond email); new channels = new adapters + normalizer, never engine changes.

    Write BOTH forms: concise at `.claude/adr/ADR-045-communication-architecture.md` (~120–160 lines, MUST/MUST NOT) and full history at `docs/adr/ADR-045-communication-architecture.md`. Cross-reference from `.claude/adr/INDEX.md`, `docs/adr/INDEX.md`, and root `CLAUDE.md` §17.

    IMPORTANT number check: the design's "ADR-033" reference is a stale R3 carryover — ADR-033 is already an unrelated accepted ADR. This ADR is **ADR-045** (038–044 occupied; owner-confirmed). Re-verify 045 is the next free slot before writing.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke platform architect. Authoritative on Communication architecture across R1 (early email), R2 (server foundation), R3 (send-side design, absorbed), and R4 (this project). Fluent in the project's concise ADR conventions (`.claude/adr/`, MUST/MUST NOT, ~120–160 lines) and the full-history form (`docs/adr/`).
  </role>

  <goal>
    ADR-045 exists in both concise (`.claude/adr/`) and full (`docs/adr/`) forms, codifying the four-part Communication decision with MUST/MUST NOT rules; indexed in both ADR INDEXes + reachable from root `CLAUDE.md` §17; passes `/adr-check` against `spec.md` with no contradiction against existing ADRs.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Every subsequent R4 wave's code review + `/adr-check` cites the Communication ADR. Landing it first (alongside the schema pass) enforces the discipline that the rest of the project references an authoritative anchor. R3 planned an "ADR-033" for the client-only send consolidation; R4 absorbs R3 and broadens the ADR to cover the full server intelligence layer + channel seams, hence a fresh number and fresh scope.

      This ADR must correctly cite its neighbors: ADR-024 (regarding family), ADR-028 (Auth v2), ADR-018 (kill-switch, for auto-file), ADR-032 (Null-Object, for feature-gated services), ADR-013 (AI facade / PublicContracts), ADR-016/014 (AI budget/cache), ADR-015 (privilege flag-only), ADR-037 (DeliverComposite), ADR-006/026/021/022/012 (Code Page + Fluent v9), ADR-029 (publish hygiene), ADR-038 (testing).
    </background>
